WEBVTT

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:03.895
A self join is not a special JOIN keyword It is a

00:00:03.921 --> 00:00:07.908
regular join where the same table is referenced
twice with different aliases

00:00:09.659 --> 00:00:12.698
Here medical staff is called s one on one side and s

00:00:12.711 --> 00:00:16.464
two on the other We match rows that belong to the
same

00:00:16.490 --> 00:00:21.903
department The second condition staff ID from s one
is less than

00:00:21.929 --> 00:00:26.510
staff ID from s two is very important Without it we
could

00:00:26.537 --> 00:00:29.945
produce both Alice-Bob and Bob-Alice and we could
even match a row

00:00:29.958 --> 00:00:36.376
to itself Run the query and inspect the colleague
pairs Notice

00:00:36.403 --> 00:00:41.706
that each pair appears only once Self joins are
useful when rows

00:00:41.719 --> 00:00:44.442
in one table need to be compared with other rows
from that

00:00:44.469 --> 00:00:49.998
same table Examples include employee-manager
relationships repeated events

00:00:50.143 --> 00:00:52.800
price comparisons and sequence analysis
